{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/499337-2e-kith-and-seeming-from-durance","id":499337,"title":"2e Kith and Seeming from Durance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-01T13:47:33-07:00","id":499337,"title":"2e Kith and Seeming from Durance","content":"Short form: the character spent twenty years (her time) playing through extended-setting versions of the laserdisc video games that were popular back in the 80s. She won her freedom by going through all the games perfectly in a long, marathon session, then got in the van of the last game's player character and drove off, out of her Keeper's Realm, into the Hedge, and finally back to Earth. In 1e, she's an Ogre (her Durance involved getting killed a lot, usually painfully), Bloodbrute kith (weaponise everything is extremely valuable in a Durance like that). But what might her 2e Kith and Seeming be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T14:42:59-07:00","id":499406,"title":"","content":"In all honesty, I have no idea. We have maybe a third of the Kiths(which may change between now and publishing) and only two Seemings. <br /> <br /> Though at least for the Seemings, the big issue is Agency, how you reclaimed yourself. Beasts shucked off all rules and restraints, becoming wild, while Darklings made a Hard Choice, sacrificing the last spark of light in themselves. So, instead of how they escaped, ask how they regained control. That should push you to what you want in a Seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T15:07:14-07:00","id":499430,"title":"","content":"We'd really need to see more of the Kiths and especially the Seemings to say. That said, Bloodbrute may make a comeback and do much the same thing, so there's that.<br /> <br /> I may be missing something, but it sounds like the Durance has a relatively &quot;planned&quot; ending the Keeper set and ultimately expected? Then it's possible the character may not get a Seeming: it's a plausible reading that the character didn't take back her agency, it was given to her.<br /> <br /> That's not a very satisfying read, though. It would help to know how all the Seemings work, and possibly some elaboration on her psychology during the Durance before a Seeming jumps out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T22:53:40-07:00","id":499872,"title":"","content":"Well Kith is supposed to now represent what your Keeper wants of your character now, why they were taken and their role in Arcadia. You should ask yourself why the Keeper took your character to Arcadia to play those games to begin with. From that, it should be fairly simple to figure what kith they'd fall under when a more full list arrives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T04:49:38-07:00","id":500145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/499337-2e-kith-and-seeming-from-durance?p=499406#post499406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all honesty, I have no idea. We have maybe a third of the Kiths(which may change between now and publishing) and only two Seemings.<br /> <br /> Though at least for the Seemings, the big issue is Agency, how you reclaimed yourself. Beasts shucked off all rules and restraints, becoming wild, while Darklings made a Hard Choice, sacrificing the last spark of light in themselves. So, instead of how they escaped, ask how they regained control. That should push you to what you want in a Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Easy, Beasts exploited the game's cheat codes to win. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T07:27:37-07:00","id":500313,"title":"","content":"Well, in her case she gained her freedom by demanding it. Actually, she earned it by being boring; she got good enough at enough things that she could get through her adventures reliably, without getting killed or severely injured, and basically said to the Keeper she knew only as a voice with no definite gender characteristics, &quot;Look. I've mastered these things, so there's no more fun you can get out of me. I do one last run, all of them, then I'm out of here. Except that this time, whatever I get in one adventure, I can keep. Through the others and after I'm done. I figure I've earned them. It's that, or I just stay here in the staging area. Your choice, voice.&quot; Given the choice between a satisfying end to a story or a tedious, long-drawn-out non-ending, the Keeper agreed to the deal, with some further negotiations to hammer out the details. At the end of Braindead 13, Karen drove out of Arcadia, and out of the Hedge, in Lance's van, seen in the final scene of that game; she chose the game order, putting that one last precisely so she could claim that van. Along with the blood sword of Iscar from Thayer's Quest, Thayer's pouch (a bag of holding), Dragonfang, Dirk's armour and some treasure from Dragon's Lair, Space Ace' blaster, and Reika Kirishima's laser pistol from Time Gal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T07:28:15-07:00","id":500323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/499337-2e-kith-and-seeming-from-durance?p=500145#post500145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Easy, Beasts exploited the game's cheat codes to win. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>That made me laugh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T08:44:10-07:00","id":500447,"title":"","content":"@LadyLens: Interesting story! If I see an appropriate Seeming posted, I'll send a link here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T10:14:18-07:00","id":500528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/499337-2e-kith-and-seeming-from-durance?p=500447#post500447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@LadyLens: Interesting story! If I see an appropriate Seeming posted, I'll send a link here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-02T22:33:50-07:00","id":501382,"title":"","content":"I'd say it does have a hint of Darkling in that tale, what with stepping on the True Fae to get out of her Durance, though there is no hint of betrayal or doing a Face-Heel turn by giving up on their past life's choices and taking a new turn there.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Ogre or Wizened will have something a bit closer for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}